rummage: local multimodal semantic search
https://github.com/av/rummage

rummage is licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE). It includes or uses the third-party
components below, under their own licences. The full list, with every Rust crate and web UI
package, is docs/LICENSES-THIRD-PARTY.md in the source repository.

In the rummage binary (statically linked):
  - llama.cpp and ggml: MIT licence, text below. https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
  - Rust crates listed in Cargo.lock, under MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, Zlib, Unicode-3.0, CC0,
    CDLA-Permissive-2.0 or MPL-2.0 (symphonia audio decoders, option-ext). MPL-2.0 source:
    https://github.com/pdeljanov/Symphonia and https://crates.io/crates/option-ext
  - SQLite (public domain, via rusqlite), libwebp (BSD-3-Clause, via libwebp-sys).
  - The web UI: Svelte (MIT), Lucide icons (ISC), clsx (MIT).
  - CUDA build only: the NVIDIA CUDA runtime (cudart_static), under the NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit
    EULA, which allows redistributing it inside applications.
    https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/eula/

Not included in the release archives (loaded from the system at run time): the Vulkan loader,
ROCm (HIP runtime, hipBLAS, rocBLAS), cuBLAS, ffmpeg, pdftotext.

The Docker images also contain, as separate programs and libraries installed from the
distribution and vendor package repositories (each package's licence is in
/usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright):
  - Ubuntu 24.04 base system (mostly GPL, LGPL, MIT and BSD licensed packages).
    Source: https://launchpad.net/ubuntu (apt-get source <package>).
  - ffmpeg 6.1 from Ubuntu, built with --enable-gpl, so licensed GPL-2.0-or-later. rummage runs
    it as a separate program and does not link it. Source: https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/ffmpeg
  - poppler-utils (pdftotext), GPL-2.0 or GPL-3.0, run as a separate program.
    Source: https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/poppler
  - vulkan image: the Vulkan loader (Apache-2.0) and Mesa's Vulkan drivers (MIT).
  - rocm image: AMD ROCm HIP runtime, hipBLAS, rocBLAS and their dependencies (MIT and other
    permissive licences) from https://repo.radeon.com.
  - cuda image: based on NVIDIA's nvidia/cuda base image, with cuBLAS, under the NVIDIA CUDA
    Toolkit EULA (https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/eula/). Using this image means accepting it.

The EmbeddingGemma 2 model (google/embeddinggemma-2) is not included. rummage downloads its
GGUF files on first use; the model is under Apache 2.0, and the Gemma prohibited use policy
applies (https://ai.google.dev/gemma/prohibited_use_policy).

